This package is an independent implementation inspired by UCSF ChimeraX.
It is not affiliated with or endorsed by UCSF, RBVI, or Schrodinger.
ChimeraX source code is not incorporated into this package. Numeric RGB data
and ideal-helix calibration coordinates refer to ChimeraX revision
8b1067a516a6d439537bcd355c3d1bdbea0f1292:
https://github.com/RBVI/ChimeraX/tree/8b1067a516a6d439537bcd355c3d1bdbea0f1292
The helix optimizer independently evaluates the published cylinder/arc objectives
with analytic gradients. Element colors use the published Jmol RGB table.

The geometric primitives in mesh.py and primitives.py are adapted from
molstar_style_in_pymol and cuemol_style_in_pymol, under the MIT License:

